' F7 -- Production deployment topology.
' Chapter 4 (Design). UML deployment diagram.
' Claim supported: the deployed system is five containers on one small VM plus
' managed Supabase, with TLS terminated by a host proxy that is not in version
' control. Notably NOT what three of the four compose files claim.
@startuml f7-deployment
!include _style.iuml

title Production deployment topology (as actually deployed)

node "Client device" as CL {
  artifact "Browser\nReact SPA (hashed assets)" as BR
}

cloud "Internet" as NET

node "**Hetzner CX23** — 4 GB / 2 vCPU, Germany" as HOST {
  artifact "**Host reverse proxy** (TLS)\n⚠ not in version control" as PROXY #DCDCDC

  node "Docker — bridge network ascend_net" as DOCK {
    artifact "**frontend**\nnginx 1.27-alpine\nstatic bundle + /api/ proxy\npublishes 127.0.0.1:3000 only" as FE
    artifact "**api**\nFastAPI, uvicorn --workers 1\n512M / 1.0 cpu\nno published port" as API
    artifact "**worker**\narq, max_jobs 4\n512M / 1.0 cpu" as WK
    database "**redis**\ncache, allkeys-lru\n256M" as RC
    queue "**redis-queue**\nbroker, noeviction + AOF\n160M" as RQ
  }
  artifact "volume redis_data" as V1
  artifact "volume redis_queue_data" as V2
}

cloud "**Supabase** (managed, external)\nPostgres 15 + pgvector\nAuth · Storage · PostgREST" as SB
cloud "**LLM providers** (external)\n7 vendors, direct HTTPS" as LLM

BR --> NET
NET --> PROXY
PROXY --> FE : "127.0.0.1:3000"
FE --> API : "proxy /api/\n**prefix NOT stripped**"
API --> RC
API --> RQ
WK --> RQ
WK --> RC
RC -- V1
RQ -- V2

API --> SB
WK --> SB
API --> LLM
WK --> LLM
BR --> SB : "auth + direct reads\n(anon key baked into bundle)"

note right of HOST
  **Container memory now sums to ~1.4 GB.**
  The LiteLLM gateway (1 GB / 0.75 vCPU) was
  removed 2026-08-25 — it had no live callers
  yet gated api and worker startup via
  depends_on: service_healthy.
end note

note bottom of DOCK
  **Traps when reading this from the repo.**
  • docker-compose.prod.yml:3 says "shared university server";
    the real host is Hetzner (docs/GDPR_DATA_PROTECTION.md:8).
    docker-compose.oracle.yml claims Oracle A1 ARM. Three files,
    three stated targets, one actual host.
  • docker-compose.staging.yml is not deployable: it sets
    network_mode host AND ports (mutually exclusive) and names
    services it never defines.
  • Dockerfile CMD says --workers 2; every compose overrides to 1.
  • Prometheus/Grafana exist in the dev compose only. /metrics is
    always exposed and unauthenticated, but nothing scrapes it in prod.
end note

legend bottom
  nginx forwards the request URI verbatim despite its own comment claiming it strips
  the /api prefix — and not stripping is what makes it work, since FastAPI mounts
  everything at /api/v1.
endlegend

@enduml
